# Interpreter-throw closure item 6, the callable-merge adapter: the model DECLARES a name and throws it; the holder's
# caller catches it with the payload (the book, section 15: a declared name is caught or listed by the caller).
# Exit 7 = 5 + the payload 2; 81 would mean the model completed.
fn: boom (int: y; int: x) int
    throws: Oops
    throw: Oops(x)
    return: 81

fn: wrap (int: k) fn: (int: x) int
    return: merge(y: k; boom)

fn: user () int
    @: w wrap(5)
    int: got 0
    ---
        got: (w: 2)
    ---
    catch: Oops (int: v)
        got: 5 + v
return: got

int: r user()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
